@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@studentId = 23127334

# HW06 verified-bug screenshot reproduction
#
# Use the VS Code REST Client extension and click "Send Request" above one request at a time.
# Before EACH bug/trial:
#   1. Stop the backend process listening on port 3000.
#   2. Start hw/eshop-sut/backend/server.js again so SQLite is recreated and seeded.
#   3. Send only the selected request.
#   4. Capture the REST Client request and response in the same screenshot.
#
# Run every bug twice after separate resets if new independent evidence is required.
# Do not add Authorization to VB-02 or VB-03: its absence is the condition being tested.

### VB-01 — Registration stores the submitted password as plaintext
# Expected by SEC-01: HTTP 200 registration, but stored password must not equal the submitted value.
# Actual defect: the database stores the exact submitted value.
# After sending, copy the generated email visible in the request and run from repository root:
# sqlite3 hw/eshop-sut/backend/database.sqlite "SELECT id,email,password FROM users WHERE email='<generated email>';"
# Capture the REST response and the real SQLite query output. Do not expose a real personal password.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-Student-Id: {{studentId}}

{
  "name": "VB01 REST Verification",
  "email": "vb01.rest.{{$timestamp}}@example.test",
  "password": "VB01Synthetic1!",
  "confirm_password": "VB01Synthetic1!"
}






















### VB-02 — Apply coupon succeeds without Authorization
# Expected by FR-09 C4 and SEC-02: reject because Authorization is absent.
# Actual defect: HTTP 200 with coupon calculation data.
# IMPORTANT: Authorization is intentionally omitted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/apply-coupon
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-Student-Id: {{studentId}}

{
  "code": "SAVE10",
  "total_amount": 500000,
  "user_id": 2
}


























### VB-03 — Product creation succeeds and persists without admin Authorization
# Expected by FR-12, SEC-02 and SEC-03: reject and create no product.
# Actual defect: HTTP 200 and a product row is created.
# IMPORTANT: Authorization is intentionally omitted.
# After sending, copy the generated name visible in the request and run from repository root:
# sqlite3 hw/eshop-sut/backend/database.sqlite "SELECT id,name,price,category_id FROM products WHERE name='<generated name>';"
# Capture the REST response and the real SQLite query output.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
X-Student-Id: {{studentId}}

{
  "name": "VB03-NOAUTH-{{$timestamp}}",
  "price": 123456,
  "description": "REST Client verification",
  "imageUrl": "https://example.test/vb03.png",
  "category_id": 1
}














### VB-04 — Coupon rejects total_amount equal to min_order_amount
# SAVE10 has min_order_amount=300000.
# Expected by FR-09 C3 (>=): equality succeeds with HTTP 200.
# Actual defect: HTTP 400 insufficient minimum value.
# The bearer value is an intentional non-secret marker. VB-02 proves this route ignores auth.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/apply-coupon
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer intentionally-present-but-unchecked
X-Student-Id: {{studentId}}

{
  "code": "SAVE10",
  "total_amount": 300000,
  "user_id": 2
}
















